  "note": "One entry per thing the Grade 6 tables say a learner must be able to do. `any` = covered when some question's stem or answer contains ANY of these phrases. `all` = covered only when ONE question contains ALL of them. Terms are matched against the question STEM AND ANSWER ONLY, never the explanation: a fact mentioned in an explanation is a fact the child is never asked. ⚠ GRADE 6 GEOGRAPHY IS LAND USE, NATURAL HAZARDS AND MAP SKILLS — nothing else. The weather and climate strand (the water cycle, windward and leeward sides, the South East Trade Winds, relief and convectional rain, temperature and altitude, climate change) is GRADE 5: its table is headed 'GRADE 5 - WEATHER' on printed page 19 and runs to page 22. Reading the extracted text rather than the pages puts that block under Grade 6, because in this PDF each grade's header sits at the FOOT of the preceding page. Do not add those facts here. ⚠ The enrichment chapters (famous figures, symbols, global connections) are deliberately absent: this ledger asks whether the pack covers the syllabus, not whether the syllabus covers the pack.",
